WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.624
One of the biggest films this summer

2
00:00:01.624 --> 00:00:03.467
is the new Planet of the Apes movie,

3
00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.950
"War for the Planet of the Apes."

4
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:05.783
(applause)

5
00:00:05.783 --> 00:00:08.443
I like that movie, now.

6
00:00:08.443 --> 00:00:12.610
And people are saying the apes in it look so realistic

7
00:00:12.669 --> 00:00:16.574
you immediately forget that they're all computer generated.

8
00:00:16.574 --> 00:00:18.622
Well, guess what, this is kinda cool

9
00:00:18.622 --> 00:00:21.574
I hired the people responsible for that technology

10
00:00:21.574 --> 00:00:24.890
and as a special treat you are about to experience

11
00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:28.016
some of that incredible CGI magic

12
00:00:28.016 --> 00:00:30.266
right here in this theater.

13
00:00:30.266 --> 00:00:32.033
Is this cool or what?

14
00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:32.949
(applause)

15
00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:33.782
Yeah!

16
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.660
Ladies and gentlemen of Comic-Con,

17
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.123
get ready to be invaded by the Planet of the Apes!

18
00:00:41.123 --> 00:00:43.801
(applause)

19
00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:46.051
(growling)

20
00:00:58.127 --> 00:00:59.465
Humans,

21
00:00:59.465 --> 00:01:00.882
bow down to apes.

22
00:01:03.991 --> 00:01:06.825
No, no, no, wait a minute

23
00:01:06.825 --> 00:01:08.833
wait a minute, stop.

24
00:01:08.833 --> 00:01:10.057
Stop!

25
00:01:10.057 --> 00:01:12.455
No, no one bow down.

26
00:01:12.455 --> 00:01:13.701
What's going on here?

27
00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:17.868
I thought we were going to see realistic, CGI apes?

28
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.641
Not a bunch of out of shape actors in green pajamas.

29
00:01:22.641 --> 00:01:23.974
What's going on?

30
00:01:25.113 --> 00:01:26.756
These not pajamas,

31
00:01:26.756 --> 00:01:29.596
these state-of-art motion capture suits.

32
00:01:29.596 --> 00:01:30.763
20 grand each.

33
00:01:31.678 --> 00:01:34.059
Human need use imagination.

34
00:01:34.059 --> 00:01:36.738
No, no, I can use my imagination.

35
00:01:36.738 --> 00:01:40.397
I paid a lot of money for this and it looks incredibly lame.

36
00:01:40.397 --> 00:01:42.493
I mean, look at that guy.

37
00:01:42.493 --> 00:01:43.866
Look at that guy right there.

38
00:01:43.866 --> 00:01:45.735
(laughter)

39
00:01:45.735 --> 00:01:47.985
(applause)

40
00:01:50.114 --> 00:01:50.947
And you!

41
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.056
You, what the hell is your name?

42
00:01:56.056 --> 00:01:57.722
My name Socate!

43
00:01:57.722 --> 00:01:59.113
(growling)

44
00:01:59.113 --> 00:02:01.696
No, no, no, forget that shit.

45
00:02:02.713 --> 00:02:05.126
What's your real name?

46
00:02:05.126 --> 00:02:06.392
Randy Schwab.

47
00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.339
(laughter)

48
00:02:07.339 --> 00:02:08.172
It's an honor to meet you.

49
00:02:08.172 --> 00:02:09.744
Big fan, big fan.

50
00:02:09.744 --> 00:02:12.079
Okay, Randy what's happening here?

51
00:02:12.079 --> 00:02:13.957
Okay, I'm a silver-back gorilla.

52
00:02:13.957 --> 00:02:16.520
About seven-feet tall, big scar right down my face,

53
00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:17.921
and this is my ape army.

54
00:02:17.921 --> 00:02:20.069
Hey man, how's it going? Nice to meet you.

55
00:02:20.069 --> 00:02:20.990
(applause)

56
00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:22.073
Real honor.

57
00:02:23.824 --> 00:02:27.491
Oh, and those guys are riding a CGI horse.

58
00:02:29.144 --> 00:02:29.977
Okay, I thought that was a giraffe.

59
00:02:29.977 --> 00:02:30.810
No, come on man, it's a horse.

60
00:02:33.247 --> 00:02:35.344
It's gonna be badass, we just need a little more time.

61
00:02:35.344 --> 00:02:37.349
Okay, how much time do you need?

62
00:02:37.349 --> 00:02:38.311
Like five, six months max.

63
00:02:38.311 --> 00:02:40.496
No, no, six months that's ridiculous.

64
00:02:40.496 --> 00:02:42.910
(grunting)

65
00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:46.179
Must protect babies from humans.

66
00:02:46.179 --> 00:02:47.012
No, no, no.

67
00:02:47.012 --> 00:02:48.531
Forget it Jessie, he's not buying it.

68
00:02:48.531 --> 00:02:49.817
Aw man.

69
00:02:49.817 --> 00:02:52.067
(laughter)

70
00:02:53.623 --> 00:02:55.873
(applause)

71
00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:01.667
Look,

72
00:03:04.474 --> 00:03:05.563
thanks for giving it a shot,

73
00:03:05.563 --> 00:03:07.332
but why don't you guys just go home, okay?

74
00:03:07.332 --> 00:03:08.973
No, but we had this really big ender

75
00:03:08.973 --> 00:03:10.681
where we put you in a massive cage.

76
00:03:10.681 --> 00:03:11.689
You put me in a big cage?

77
00:03:11.689 --> 00:03:13.973
Yeah, you'll love it. Okay guys, ape up.

78
00:03:13.973 --> 00:03:16.104
(growling)

79
00:03:16.104 --> 00:03:20.195
Human cannot visit us, lower the cage!

80
00:03:20.195 --> 00:03:23.195
(suspenseful music)

81
00:03:24.353 --> 00:03:26.603
(applause)

82
00:03:35.131 --> 00:03:37.995
No, no this is really stupid.

83
00:03:37.995 --> 00:03:38.828
I'm sorry.

84
00:03:38.828 --> 00:03:40.629
Use your imagination!

85
00:03:40.629 --> 00:03:42.742
No, I'm not going to use my imagination.

86
00:03:42.742 --> 00:03:44.132
I'm not going to do that.

87
00:03:44.132 --> 00:03:45.783
Human has escaped!

88
00:03:45.783 --> 00:03:47.491
Human has escaped!

89
00:03:47.491 --> 00:03:49.908
(screeching)

